meta-cubie-robot
================

Yocto (scarthgap) product layer for robots on the Radxa Cubie A7S: the QB OS
distro and the images, on top of the meta-cubie-a7s board layer.

Unofficial community project, not made, endorsed or supported by Radxa,
Allwinner, Imagination Technologies, VeriSilicon, the Yocto Project or any
other company or project whose software it builds.


Dependencies
------------

Required:

  URI: https://git.yoctoproject.org/poky
  branch: scarthgap
  layers: meta

  meta-cubie-a7s (same repo)

Optional, enables the ROS 2 Jazzy images (dynamic-layers/meta-ros):

  URI: https://github.com/ros/meta-ros
  branch: scarthgap
  layers: meta-ros-common, meta-ros2, meta-ros2-jazzy

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded
  branch: scarthgap
  layers: meta-oe, meta-python

  URI: https://github.com/kraj/meta-clang
  branch: scarthgap

Optional, adds Docker to the ROS images (dynamic-layers/meta-virtualization):

  URI: https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-virtualization
  branch: scarthgap

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded
  branch: scarthgap
  layers: meta-oe, meta-python, meta-networking, meta-filesystems


Distro
------

  DISTRO = "qb"

QB OS, started from oe-core's defaultsetup.conf as the Yocto manual suggests:
sysvinit, rpm packages, Poky's hardening flags, uninative and hash equivalence,
no ptest. See conf/distro/qb.conf.


Images
------

  cubie-a7s-image-base   minimal image, no ROS (release)
  cubie-a7s-image-playground
                         base plus NPU samples (tim-vx-lenet), CedarC codec demos and
                         GStreamer test sources, kmscube, glmark2, vulkaninfo and clinfo
                         for experimenting (dev)
  cubie-a7s-image        ROS 2 Jazzy + Zenoh, needs the meta-ros layers (release)
  cubie-a7s-image-dev    same as cubie-a7s-image (dev)

The ROS images also get Docker when meta-virtualization is in bblayers. It is off at
boot: /etc/init.d/docker.init start, or update-rc.d docker.init defaults to start it
at every boot.

All of them include the board's drivers and firmware, wifi (wpa-supplicant, iw), an
SSH server, ONNX Runtime with the NPU provider, GStreamer with the hardware codecs
and the GPU stack. The first boot grows the root partition and filesystem to fill the
SD card, once (recipes-core/rootfs-grow).
With meta-networking in bblayers they also set the clock from the network with chrony
(`chronyc tracking` shows the state).

Set in build/conf/site.conf (not tracked):

  WIFI_SSID, WIFI_PSK            wlan0 connects at boot
  CUBIE_SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEYS      public key file for root over SSH
  CUBIE_ROOT_PASSWORD_HASH       `openssl passwd -6` output, for the serial console

Release images need at least one of the two logins, the build fails otherwise, and
also fails if debug-tweaks reaches a release image. SSH takes keys only. Dev images
have passwordless root and dnf, never ship those.


Building
--------

  source poky/oe-init-build-env build
  bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-cubie-a7s ../meta-cubie-robot
  MACHINE=cubie-a7s DISTRO=qb bitbake cubie-a7s-image-base


